---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---
<Layout
  title="Company Registration Walkthrough"
  description="The actual steps to register a company in Dubai, from choosing an activity to receiving your trade licence."
>
  <section class="container">
    <p class="eyebrow">Registration</p>
    <h1>Registering your company, step by step</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      The sequence is broadly the same whether you're registering in a free
      zone or on the mainland — what varies is who reviews each step and how
      long approvals take.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="container">
    <ol class="steps">
      <li>
        <strong>Choose your business activity.</strong> This determines which
        zones or mainland categories you're even eligible for, and it's the
        single most common place founders lose time by picking too narrow or
        too broad an activity code.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Choose your structure and jurisdiction.</strong> Free zone,
        mainland, or offshore — see the
        <a href="/free-zones/">free zone comparison</a> and
        <a href="/mainland/">mainland guide</a> if you haven't already.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Reserve a trade name</strong> and submit initial approval —
        usually the fastest step, often same-day.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Submit licence application and documents</strong> — passport
        copies, business plan (for some activities), and, for mainland,
        a Memorandum of Association.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Sign the lease or flexi-desk agreement</strong> required by
        your jurisdiction, then receive your trade licence.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Apply for visas</strong> (yourself and any employees) once
        the licence is issued.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Open a business bank account</strong> — start this early;
        see <a href="/banking/">banking</a> for why it's rarely the fast
        step people expect.
      </li>
    </ol>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .steps { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--space-2); padding-left: 1.2em; }
  .steps li { max-width: 65ch; }
</style>
